    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19617" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glaesum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glēsum</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glessum</span></b> ), i, n.
		cf. Germ. Glas; gleissen = glänzen, to glimmer; Engl.
			glass, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>amber</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. G. 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 37, 3,
				11, § 42</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glaesārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of amber</i>, <i>amber-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insula,</span>”
				<i>which produces amber</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 13, 27, § 97</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">37, 3, 11,
				§ 42</span></i>.</div>
